<!--
  AI-assisted: Claude Opus 5.5 (xhigh effort) via Claude Code, 2026-10-10: wrote the URDF/xacro, launch file and tests.
  AI-assisted: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code, 2026-10-16: drew the plate's rounded front (front_slices, from the
  classmate's plate CAD in the private course repo (plate CAD is not published here)) and updated the plate comments for the CAD outline.
  AI-assisted: Claude Opus 5.5 (xhigh effort) via Cursor, 2026-10-29: added the power bank (box power_bank, colour
  bank_black, guards) from the M1.T16 readings and updated the mass, centre-of-mass, inertia and Module 6 comments;
  after a review the same day, added the one-weighing guard, the body_box size check, the bank-floor guard and the
  complete bank/motor overlap test, compared the bank top with the measured rear underside, and corrected the inertia,
  Isaac massless-link, self-collision and wheel-layout comments and added the M2.T16 notes (bank, caster); later the
  same day, after Xiaohui's footprint decision, ended the ESP32-CAM box at esp32_front_x and added the two visual-only
  cable boxes (body_visual_box, colour cable_grey); after a review of that, gave the front cable a collider (an agent
  decision for Xiaohui to accept), added the footprint guards and the floor check of body_visual_box, and stated the
  rear wall-contact offset, the camera-view occlusion and what is not modelled.

  beaconmind_car.urdf.xacro: the robot description of Xiaohui Chen's two-wheel car for the BeaconMind course project
  (robot_state_publisher TF tree, C12; Isaac Sim twin, M2.T4 / M2.T16).
  Until 2026-10-29 the Module 6 Gazebo Fortress lab (assignments/assignment6 in the private course repo, wrapped with the
  instructor's <gazebo> blocks) included this file directly. Since 2026-10-29 the lab mounts a frozen snapshot instead
  (assignments/assignment6/beaconmind_description-m6-snapshot in the private course repo), so changes here no longer
  reach the lab.

  Frames (README C1): base_link = midpoint between the drive-wheel centres AT AXLE HEIGHT (z = 0 at the axle);
  +x toward the camera lens / caster end (the front); +y = robot left; +z up. Floor is at z = -wheel_radius.
  Every number comes from two files in this folder: car_props.xacro, GENERATED by beaconmind_description/gen_props.py
  from configs/car.json (M1.T9; never edit it by hand), and car_geometry_extras.xacro, hand-written, for the geometry
  car.json does not carry (plate outline, part boxes, part masses). Both label each value measured / derived /
  ESTIMATE / ASSUMED / stand-in. The camera pose stays provisional until configs/camera.json (M1.T7) exists.

  Links (exactly): base_link, chassis_link, left_wheel_link, right_wheel_link, caster_link, camera_link,
  camera_optical_frame, imu_link.
  This file has NO <gazebo>, <sensor>, ray or lidar elements (D1a: no range sensor). Simulator-specific
  blocks belong in a wrapper (for the lab: assignments/assignment6/lab-step10/gazebo_car.urdf.xacro, private repo).
-->
<robot name="beaconmind_car">
  <!-- ================= base_link: the axle midpoint (no visual, no inertia) ================= -->
  <!-- No <inertial> here on purpose: KDL (robot_state_publisher) does not support an inertia on the root link,
       so the body's mass lives in chassis_link, attached by a fixed joint.
       Isaac Sim (M2.T16): base_link and camera_optical_frame are the two links with NO <inertial> (no mass). With
       merge_fixed_joints = False the Isaac URDF importer makes both of them bodies and logs, for each, the warnings
       "No mass specified for link %s" and "Link %s has no colliders, and no inertia was imported; assigning a small
       isotropic inertia matrix" (isaacsim.asset.importer.urdf 2.4.30 in the Spark's Isaac Sim source,
       plugins/isaacsim.asset.importer.urdf/UrdfImporter.cpp lines 393 and 608; read 2026-10-29). So EXPECT those two
       warnings for these two links. M2.T16 checks that their PhysX mass is negligible, that the car's total stays
       0.660 kg (car.json mass_kg), and that no OTHER warning mentions them. What mass PhysX assigns them is NOT
       verified here. (In the Gazebo lab, sdformat's URDF converter merges fixed-joint links into their parent by
       default, so these frames get no body of their own there.) -->
  <link name="base_link"/>
